rows.en:
But it seemed like nothing short of reckless.
In both temperament and build, {f:there was just no way Arai could ever beat Kazama.|there was no way Arai could ever beat Kazama, was there?}
Arai was hunched forward, his head pressed into Kazama's stomach.
"What are you doing☆"
Even as Kazama pounded on his back, Arai endured it and wouldn't let go.{p}

Before long, Kazama's face changed color.
Greasy sweat was beading on his forehead.
"Stop it! Let go of me☆"
Was being squeezed that tight hurting him{f:?|?}
He grabbed Arai by the hair and tried to pry him off.
But Arai wouldn't come loose.{p}

Kazama's scream rang out.
This was no longer something a human being could do.
Tearing open a living person's stomach with your teeth, shirt and all... no human could do that{f:.|.}{p}

"Oh, come on, {c}{f:|}.
You don't seriously think I'd actually lay a hand on him, do you?"
Kazama was trying to keep his tone light, but his eyes weren't smiling.{p}

It would be terrible if one of them got hurt{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} decided to stop them.
"Please stop!"
With help from the others, we somehow managed to pull the two of them apart.{p}

"This is bad.
The spirit is using Kazama as a medium to break the barrier I put up around this room."
Arai's dark, introverted personality had completely changed; he was brimming with energy.{p}

"With my power, putting a barrier around this room was the best I could do.
That's why I tried to drive the spirits off, even a little, while all of you were telling your stories, but then that happened...
It looks like we have no choice but to fight."{p}

The Arai back then was apparently a different person from the real Arai, who came later.
What on earth {f:was|was} yesterday's incident?
Maybe when Kazama released that mysterious power, it drove the spirit away{f:...?|...}
There were so many things I didn't understand{f:.|.}
{f:This school|I}{f: is full of countless mysteries.| quit the newspaper club.}
{f:I|Even if only for a moment}{f: could feel in my bones that I'd better not touch those mysteries.|, I had tried to sacrifice Hino, and I hated myself for it...}{p}{f:I'd had|I've had} enough of the seven wonders.{p}

{f:I|I} didn't stop them.
No, to be precise, I couldn't stop them{f:.|.}
Kazama and Arai {f:were|were} both dead serious.
I could sense that each of them truly hated the other.
The hatred wasn't aimed at {f:me|me}, but it still gave me goosebumps.
I'd never known other people's emotions could be so raw.
Suddenly, a girl screamed.
Surprisingly, {f:it was Arai who swung first.|it seemed Arai was the one who swung first.}
Arai's punch grazed Kazama's cheek.{p}

"You bastard!"
It wasn't a very powerful punch, but it seemed to make Kazama snap.
With a ferocity you'd never imagine from his usual self, he punched Arai.{p}

Kazama's face was deathly pale.
No wonder{f:.|.}
To become a murderer at such a young age.
But then Kazama said something outrageous.{p}

When he put it that way, I had no comeback{f:.|.}
If {f:I|I} had stopped them, this would never have happened{f:.|...}
Everyone seemed to feel the same way, and no one argued any further.
{f:We|We} were accomplices{f:.|...}
Before I knew it, that's how I had come to feel.
"Let's take him to the incinerator."
Someone suggested it.
...It seemed like a very good idea.{p}

{f:We|We} decided to carry Arai's body to the incinerator.
Of course, there was no way one person could do it alone{f:.|.}
It would be best for several of us to lift him together{f:.|.}{p}{f:As for the girls,|It's scary,} {f:I'll have them check that no one's around,|but I have to help...} {f:so what should I do|so where should I hold him}?
